OL,3,GNEWSABereaved dad who 'lost running
OL,4,Aspirit' to run GNR
OL,5,
OL,6,FA father who lost his "running spirit"
OL,7,Fwhen his teenage children took their
OL,8,Fown lives separately, within the space
OL,9,Fof a year, is preparing to return to
OL,10,Fthe Great North Run (GNR).
OL,12,FDavid Beadle, 45, from Shildon in
OL,13,FCounty Durham, lost his 17-year-old
OL,14,Fdaughter, Quinn, in 2018. Ten months
OL,15,Flater, his son Dyllon, 21, also took
OL,16,Fhis own life.
OL,18,FBeadle had been a keen runner, having
OL,19,Fcompleted the annual half-marathon
OL,20,Feight times, but he felt unable to take
OL,21,Fafter the loss of his children until
OL,22,F"something changed" this year.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,392,390,260,160,0,100
